{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following","id":1213232,"title":"Has this game gained a fairly noticeable following","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-29T17:27:01-07:00","id":1213232,"title":"Has this game gained a fairly noticeable following","content":"Just wondering. I really think this is a very unique edition to the chronicles of darkness and have read the corebook PDF, (can't find a free players guide though) and it would be a real shame to see this game get no new edition due to people overreacting after they did many of its problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:02:36-07:00","id":1213264,"title":"","content":"Considering this sub-forum has been fairly active, I'd say yes, it has a following.<br /> <br /> Speaking for myself: the ideas and themes in Beast were always solid. I think it was the presentation of the game was what turned people off. But thankfully the newer releases have been doing a better job at making the intriguing ideas and themes clearer, especially the recently released Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> This game appealing to some but not to others is nothing new to me. That's the big draw with Chronicles of Darkness (and by extension World of Darkness): the different gamelines have something for everyone to dig into and have fun with. Me personally: while I dig the hell out of Beast, Changeling, Demon, and Werewolf, I find Mage to be a little intimidating for me to dive right into and Vampire was always a tough sell because I don't find playing as vampires to be all that interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 04-29-2018, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T19:47:32-07:00","id":1213281,"title":"","content":"There's definitely a following.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast is a 2e game. It's not due for a new edition, because it was made for the current edition. If there's a Chronicles of Darkness 3rd edition, I doubt Beast will be skipped for an update, but that's a long way aways unless something drastic happens behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:16:13-07:00","id":1213296,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer! It's just i was real worried this game was not gonna be realized for how it is. Luckily it seems to have the opposite of hype backlash where it was called bad but ended up being good if you give it a chance<br /> <br /> Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, do y'all know why it still gets some hate by the overall community","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 04-29-2018, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:23:00-07:00","id":1213299,"title":"","content":"In addition to a Player's Guide, Beast has a Night Horrors book, a fiction anthology, and assorted Dark Eras (including a Thousand and One Nights and the Necropolis at Hawara).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:39:24-07:00","id":1213305,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, night horrors? I'm gonna be honest I've only got to read the corebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:41:35-07:00","id":1213306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213296#post1213296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, do y'all know why it still gets some hate by the overall community</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the corebook, on the technical level it was a bit of a mess. It's one of the few big books where a rewrite of the corebook has happened. Unfortunately, they weren't as thorough as they would and in the final book there were still some artifacts left from the previous version. Which causes some odd clashes and confusion between the fluff and crunch.<br /> <br /> The main issue is that the corebook presents the Beasts as serial abusers from Feeding. The type that delights in causing mental and emotional trauma in other people. And unlike the other CofD splats, they either can't take as many convenient shortcuts (for instance, Vampire having blood dolls and ghouls being consensual donors of blood, or subsisting off of blood bags) or it's just not optional (Demon's Pact system).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:46:22-07:00","id":1213310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213305#post1213305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, night horrors? I'm gonna be honest I've only got to read the corebook</div> </div> </div> </div>Night Horrors is a line that has antagonists for various game lines. The Beast one was called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1030158-conquering-heroes\">Conquering Heroes</a>. There's a section of Hero antagonists, a section on Beast antagonists, and a new group called the Insatiable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T21:00:45-07:00","id":1213317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213306#post1213306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the case of the corebook, on the technical level it was a bit of a mess. It's one of the few big books where a rewrite of the corebook has happened. Unfortunately, they weren't as thorough as they would and in the final book there were still some artifacts left from the previous version. Which causes some odd clashes and confusion between the fluff and crunch.<br /> <br /> The main issue is that the corebook presents the Beasts as serial abusers from Feeding. The type that delights in causing mental and emotional trauma in other people. And unlike the other CofD splats, they either can't take as many convenient shortcuts (for instance, Vampire having blood dolls and ghouls being consensual donors of blood, or subsisting off of blood bags) or it's just not optional (Demon's Pact system).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I know what you mean by artifacts <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a>, like the woman who wants men to touch her so she can break their bones, right?<br /> <br /> Also thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> (so no actually need to do name tags for y'all to see I posted something toward you)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T22:04:10-07:00","id":1213330,"title":"","content":"As to the controversy that strongly hangs around the game:<br /> <br /> I've consistently felt there's a &quot;can't see the forest for the trees&quot; issue. People get wrapped up in a specific analogy, example, or whatever, and ignore the context it is meant to be in.<br /> <br /> Beast is very much a game about cyclical violence. Beasts are the half the recognizes this and thus has the power to try to subvert it, while Heroes are the half that doubles down into the cycle. The problem is when using real world examples, Beasts and Heroes can be either &quot;side&quot; of a repeated violence. Beasts are both in many ways outsiders for things beyond their control and victims of circumstance, and abusers that perpetuate violence and pain. <br /> <br /> So when you try to say that a Beast finding their true identity after being haunted by their Horror in their Dream before the Devouring is like a trans people trying to figure out their identity, we see a lot of people then jump on that as trying to say, &quot;Oh so the means trans people are violent abusers.&quot; <br /> <br /> When you use hate groups to help explain the psychology of Heroes, people look at how Beasts tend to create their own Heroes via irresponsible feeding, and say, &quot;oh, the book is saying the KKK exists because of black people not being perfect.&quot;<br /> <br /> And really, once that impression sunk in, it's justifiably hard to shake people out of it. There's nothing anyone could say to get me to play MYFAROG... there's nothing in my mind that could separate the game (if you don't know about it, warning, it's not a fun thing to look into esp. re: racism, antisemitism, murder, and arson). from it's creator and the content he added because he's who he is. Maybe there's a great wonderful RPG if you cut out a few pages, but I'm never going to care to learn that, and I can't imagine anything someone can say that would disabuse me of my stance.<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't have the same issues as that in terms of content, but there's enough messy spots in the language that can turn people off the book, and they have no responsibility to us to change their impression. I can do my best to try to advocate a fair reading in public (like these forums) but I'm not going to blame people for getting the wrong message from the text as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T22:25:09-07:00","id":1213332,"title":"","content":"There's also a number of people who have made or are making fan Dark Eras for Beast, which takes a lot of time commitment. I'd say that's a strong indicator the game has a following and that those who like it are very passionate about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T22:33:33-07:00","id":1213334,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I've never thought of it that way, I can see how many would be turned off by it<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4433_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4433\" data-vbnamecard=\"4433\">Second Chances</a> that's awesome! I did not know there were people that commited to the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T00:21:49-07:00","id":1213346,"title":"","content":"I was one of the guys interested in concept of <b>Beast</b> gameline, but turn off by mess of the corebook. Now, with <b>Beast Player's Guide</b> that I end reading, I can assert you whole gameline is <i>very</i> solid as whole. I was frown upon by making many topics about it lately, to clear a large portions of setting to me, but I think you can look on them and get more coherent view of the game. Just see links below. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193420-i-want-to-run-a-beast-but-do-not-know-what-to-do\">I want to run a Beast - but do not know what to do</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209162-what-brood-can-do-together\">What brood can do together </a>( i.e. chronicles ideas )<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies\">Horrors from mythologies</a> ( NPCs ideas )<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1209701-beasts-interactions-with-lair-how-to\">Beasts interactions with Lair HOW-TO</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1210496-primordial-cults-inspirations-sample-cults-etc\">Primordial Cults inspirations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1193199-bpg-inguma-%E2%80%93-family-of-outsiders-%E2%80%93-and-minorities\">Inguma - Family of Outsiders</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213217-soundtracks-of-beasts\">Soundtracks of Beasts</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T04:27:47-07:00","id":1213374,"title":"","content":"The following was always there, and consisted of passionate and dedicated people, but it's growing. The Player's Guide did wonders and it's being in a solid place since release when it comes to sells (at least judging from DriveThru RPG's list of bestselling titles). There was quite a bit of trepidation for it, and the weeks before the release were like taking a deep breath before a jump, but the book delivered what it promised and even more.<br /> <br /> I think Beast's in a good spot right now and that future's looks bright","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T06:00:00-07:00","id":1213396,"title":"","content":"I can only add that Beast Player's Guide IS LITERALLY Game Changer. In my POV, BPG should simply be called 'BtP corebook 2', it's how much it changes and expand even in fundametal elements of game. Really, first thing you do after getting BtP corebook is buying BPG, best at once. Get this book - right now! \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T06:13:12-07:00","id":1213399,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everyone who participated in this thread, very happy to have a helpful, welcome, and interactive community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T06:42:34-07:00","id":1213407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213330#post1213330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to the controversy that strongly hangs around the game:<br /> <br /> I've consistently felt there's a &amp;quot;can't see the forest for the trees&amp;quot; issue. People get wrapped up in a specific analogy, example, or whatever, and ignore the context it is meant to be in.<br /> <br /> Beast is very much a game about cyclical violence. Beasts are the half the recognizes this and thus has the power to try to subvert it, while Heroes are the half that doubles down into the cycle. The problem is when using real world examples, Beasts and Heroes can be either &amp;quot;side&amp;quot; of a repeated violence. Beasts are both in many ways outsiders for things beyond their control and victims of circumstance, and abusers that perpetuate violence and pain. <br /> <br /> So when you try to say that a Beast finding their true identity after being haunted by their Horror in their Dream before the Devouring is like a trans people trying to figure out their identity, we see a lot of people then jump on that as trying to say, &amp;quot;Oh so the means trans people are violent abusers.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> When you use hate groups to help explain the psychology of Heroes, people look at how Beasts tend to create their own Heroes via irresponsible feeding, and say, &amp;quot;oh, the book is saying the KKK exists because of black people not being perfect.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And really, once that impression sunk in, it's justifiably hard to shake people out of it. There's nothing anyone could say to get me to play MYFAROG... there's nothing in my mind that could separate the game (if you don't know about it, warning, it's not a fun thing to look into esp. re: racism, antisemitism, murder, and arson). from it's creator and the content he added because he's who he is. Maybe there's a great wonderful RPG if you cut out a few pages, but I'm never going to care to learn that, and I can't imagine anything someone can say that would disabuse me of my stance.<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't have the same issues as that in terms of content, but there's enough messy spots in the language that can turn people off the book, and they have no responsibility to us to change their impression. I can do my best to try to advocate a fair reading in public (like these forums) but I'm not going to blame people for getting the wrong message from the text as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, this eloquently scratches that long-time itch. Seriously, we need to nail this to the heads of certain people or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T07:33:45-07:00","id":1213423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213407#post1213407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, this eloquently scratches that long-time itch. Seriously, we need to nail this to the heads of certain people or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll get someone to write it out on an ofuda for ease of nailing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T08:21:00-07:00","id":1213437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213423#post1213423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll get someone to write it out on an ofuda for ease of nailing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a plan","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T10:05:21-07:00","id":1213474,"title":"","content":"While others already explained what caused the majority of the outrage, there is a secondary reason that made some people disappointed with the Corebook. The game advertises itself as letting you play a legendary monster, but in practice the monster is an external entity that latches itself onto you. If you starve yourself, it can roam the Dream and act independently of you. If you overfeed it, it can fall asleep and leave you mostly human. For many this brought a sense of separation between the character and the Horror and those readers felt like it wasn't what they were promised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T12:19:17-07:00","id":1213502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213299#post1213299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In addition to a Player's Guide, Beast has a Night Horrors book, a fiction anthology, and assorted Dark Eras (including a Thousand and One Nights and the Necropolis at Hawara).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is also Building A Legend; a very good campaign starter even for not Beast.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213474#post1213474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While others already explained what caused the majority of the outrage, there is a secondary reason that made some people disappointed with the Corebook. The game advertises itself as letting you play a legendary monster, but in practice the monster is an external entity that latches itself onto you. If you starve yourself, it can roam the Dream and act independently of you. If you overfeed it, it can fall asleep and leave you mostly human. For many this brought a sense of separation between the character and the Horror and those readers felt like it wasn't what they were promised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although the Kickstarter re-writes actually enforced that separation more with the change from Homecoming to Devouring, so it would seem some people had the opposite feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T13:05:34-07:00","id":1213512,"title":"","content":"The re-writes certainly did that, but I can only speculate what the intent behind it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T14:55:13-07:00","id":1213537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213512#post1213512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The re-writes certainly did that, but I can only speculate what the intent behind it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I think the bigger issue for the crowd you mentioned was the lack of a general 'Beast' form in the real world (although I contend that opening a Primordial Pathway is that made more interesting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:12:00-07:00","id":1213640,"title":"","content":"I do get people wanting to play creatures more physically, and thus not being into how Beast touches on that. Though the game never really sold itself as anything but what it is. The first blog post on the main page directly says the game is about people with monster souls (also we don't have to speculate that much on the purpose of the re-writes, there was a blog post all about it). .<br /> <br /> Though really, having played a low Satiety strategy character with Atavisms as a main focus... you feel pretty damned like your horror's archetype even if you don't visually look it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:43:16-07:00","id":1213651,"title":"","content":"Plus can't you just start a session on the highest level (forgot what they called it) and be incarnates, that way they can be a monster in the physical world right away instead of having to keep working toward that goal and sorting about getting killed or having a different inheritance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T21:57:57-07:00","id":1213671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213537#post1213537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the bigger issue for the crowd you mentioned was the lack of a general 'Beast' form in the real world (although I contend that opening a Primordial Pathway is that made more interesting).</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why we have <i>Skin Deep</i> Atavism in <b>Beast Player's Guide</b> - it let's you PHYSICALLY change your human character to get some fantastic traits of yours Horror. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And that was one of 'fixes' I needed myself to appreciate the game - look on my Horrors <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1208030-horrors-from-mythologies\">from mythologies</a> topic - half of shown monsters I written in there have <i>Skin Deep</i> power with a reason... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2018, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T22:06:35-07:00","id":1213672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213651#post1213651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus can't you just start a session on the highest level (forgot what they called it) and be incarnates, that way they can be a monster in the physical world right away instead of having to keep working toward that goal and sorting about getting killed or having a different inheritance</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without homebrewing: as of right now there are no official rules for playable Incarnates- or any of the Inheritances for that matter.<br /> <br /> And all the published material as of right now state that being any of the Inheritances would alter the themes of Beasts too much to mesh with the regular setting and rulesets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T12:51:54-07:00","id":1213864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1213672#post1213672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not without homebrewing: as of right now there are no official rules for playable Incarnates- or any of the Inheritances for that matter.<br /> <br /> And all the published material as of right now state that being any of the Inheritances would alter the themes of Beasts too much to mesh with the regular setting and rulesets.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could play an Insatiable, they have more information on them that would enable playing them more easily than playing one of the Inheritances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T14:31:19-07:00","id":1213890,"title":"","content":"I must have missed the part where the Incarnates are not playable, because the stuff in the core is pretty comprehensive as that goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T14:41:27-07:00","id":1213895,"title":"","content":"That's what I was thinking, but they say it's really more so you get an interactive epilogue to show the &quot;happy&quot; ending for you character","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T06:58:49-07:00","id":1214142,"title":"","content":"Even without the endgame evolutions of Beasts, you can always bring people into your lair and merge with your Horror there. I could see a scenario where you chase/ get chased through the alleys of the city until they come to a dead end with a door, and that door leads to the chamber of your lair associated with that alley. The prey go through, and now they're really out of luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:31:22-07:00","id":1214150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1213232-has-this-game-gained-a-fairly-noticeable-following?p=1214142#post1214142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even without the endgame evolutions of Beasts, you can always bring people into your lair and merge with your Horror there. I could see a scenario where you chase/ get chased through the alleys of the city until they come to a dead end with a door, and that door leads to the chamber of your lair associated with that alley. The prey go through, and now they're really out of luck.</div> </div> </div> </div>Illusion of Safety is basically that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> A burrow straight to the heart, and no die rolling to see if it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24132-iceben","name":"IceBen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}